{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792178321,"nonce":"z8d8y1qhFZlQvZWNTx+aEiukTOg=","title":"README: a live banner after the intro, an EV dashboard in light and dark","message":"**What**\n\nAn animated GIF between the `# ashui` intro and Usage, distinct from the Showcase section: an EV's dashboard as one scene. A car modelled in code stands in a studio that follows the theme, under floating glass panels styled as ChimpMonk's editor styles its own (the elevated surface a third opaque over a 12px saturated blur, the theme border and large shadow, squircle corners). The gauges are drawn on canvases: a speedometer, a segmented battery, a climate dial and an energy curve. A dock of Remix icons sits at the bottom.\n\n**Decisions so far**\n\n- No stock car model. The only one at hand (Sketchfab's Ginetta Akula) is CC-BY-NC-SA, which does not sit well inside an Apache-2.0 project's own banner.\n- The car is silver all through, with dark glass and gunmetal trim; it need not follow the theme's colours.\n- Panels only read as glass when something with colour is behind them: an accent-coloured light pool under the car reaches under the dock and the side panels.\n- Custom canvas widgets, not stock progress bars, for anything a dashboard draws.\n\n**Remaining**\n\n- Model the car on the subdivision cage (ea32c0c): real wheel arches and window openings, creased character lines, one surface with paint, glass and trim slots.\n- Detail pass over every panel: typography, gauge ticks and labels, states, icons, spacing.\n- The animation: a slow turntable, gauges ticking, light and dark cross-faded. Then the README insert.\n\nScene: tools/snapshot/scenes/Banner.hx and Banner.css.","files":null}]}